  "result": "Perfect! I've found and fixed the bug. The issue was in `src/server/services/project-service.ts` at line 50.\n\n**The Problem:**\nThe code was calling `wouldExceedLimit(org.plan, \"projects\", used, 0)` with an explicit `0` for the `requested` parameter. This meant it was checking `used + 0 > limit` (i.e., `used > limit`), which is off by one.\n\n**The Fix:**\nChanged it to `wouldExceedLimit(org.plan, \"projects\", used)` which uses the default `requested = 1` parameter, so it correctly checks `used + 1 > limit`.\n\n**Example with a free plan (limit = 2 projects):**\n- Before fix: `used > 2` allowed users to create a 3rd project (wrong)\n- After fix: `used + 1 > 2` blocks creation when they already have 2 projects (correct)\n\nI also fixed the error message to display the actual limit instead of the current usage count.",
